From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: theme the external shell's tray clock

Purpose: draw the XP tray clock on the notification area's background with
the Clock theme's font and colour.
Wine before: the native clock's theme handle was closed after
SetWindowTheme and its paint fell back to opaque text.
Change: subclass the clock: call its original WM_PAINT, which also updates
the formatted window text, then draw the notification area background and
the text with a theme handle of our own. Input and timers stay native; the
subclass and theme are revalidated after the original paint.
Evidence: tests/clock-theme.c, tests/clock-metrics.c, tests/clock-pixels.c.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
Old patches: 0019.
---
 dlls/uxtheme/Makefile.in  |   1 +
 dlls/uxtheme/clock.c      | 153 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/uxtheme/system.c     |   1 +
 dlls/uxtheme/uxthemedll.h |   2 +
 4 files changed, 157 insertions(+)

